What / How: How AI Agents Help Reduce Manual Effort

The IPDV agent coordinates the verification workflow and evidence collection, working with specialized agents to reduce manual effort in repetitive operations, execution tracking, and result consolidation:
- DSIM Owner: Handles regression setup, compilation, job tracking, and test-result classification.
- SMA CRV/DSIM Debug: Analyzes logs and waveforms, identifies failure causes, and helps resolve test-side issues. RTL issues are referred to the design owner.
- OpenTitan Coverage Closure: Analyzes coverage gaps, adds tests, and iteratively runs simulations to help achieve coverage closure.
- Coverage Merge: Automatically merges VDB files, loads exclusion lists (EL), and consolidates coverage scores.
- DVC CyberSecurity: Periodically collects cybersecurity metrics and uploads them to the DVP server.
Resource / Quality: Targeting at Least a 20% Reduction in Manual Effort

This automation frees up engineering time spent on regression operations, initial debugging, coverage merging, and report consolidation, allowing engineers to focus on new-feature verification, corner-case planning, and critical issue analysis.

It also helps ensure that verification tasks are rerun after each revision, reducing the risk of missed runs and the reuse of outdated evidence.
